              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em What lattice theorists can do for superstring/M-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.05421"} arXiv:1604.05421
          %p
            With strong
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+fields"} background fields
          %ul
            %li
              Gergely Endrodi,
              %em QCD with background electromagnetic fields on the lattice: a review
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.19780"}> arXiv:2406.19780
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher
            lattice gauge theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joe+Huxford"}> Joe Huxford
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The higher lattice gauge theory model for topological phases of matter
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://ora.ox.ac.uk/objects/uuid:e789bf29-179b-4b79-9168-605bf8c035ba"} uuid:e789bf29-179b-4b79-9168-605bf8c035ba
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://ora.ox.ac.uk/objects/uuid:e789bf29-179b-4b79-9168-605bf8c035ba/files/ddj52w5202"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joe+Huxford"}> Joe Huxford
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+H.+Simon"} Steven H. Simon
                %em Excitations in the Higher Lattice Gauge Theory Model for Topological Phases I: Overview
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.08294"}> arXiv:2202.08294
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Further on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher
            lattice gauge theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Orendain"}> Juan Orendain
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+A.+Zapata"} José A. Zapata
                %em Higher homotopy and lattice gauge fields
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.02363"}> arXiv:2311.02363
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
                , Lev Spodyneiko:
                %em Higher symmetries, anomalies, and crossed squares in lattice gauge theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.16966"}> arXiv:2507.16966
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Comparison to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
          %ul
            %li#KovenskySchmitt24
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Kovensky"}> Nicolas Kovensky
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Schmitt"} Andreas Schmitt
              %em Thermal pion condensation: holography meets lattice QCD
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.12641"}> arXiv:2407.12641
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesMontoCarloSimulations Computer simulations
          %p Introduction:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masanori+Hanada"}> Masanori Hanada
                ,
                %em Markov Chain Monte Carlo for Dummies
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.08490"}> arXiv:1808.08490
                )
            %li
              %p
                Anosh Joseph,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Markov Chain Monte Carlo Methods in Quantum Field Theories: A Modern Primer
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.10997"} arXiv:1912.10997
          %p
            Account of computer simulation results in lattice
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
          %ul
            %li#FodorHoelbling12
              Zoltan Fodor, Christian Hoelbling, sections II-IV of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Light Hadron Masses from Lattice QCD
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1203.4789"} arXiv:1203.4789
          %p
            The idea of using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monte+Carlo+method"} Monte Carlo method
            for lattice gauge theory originates with:
          %ul
            %li#Creutz79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Creutz"}> Michael Creutz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Confinement and the Critical Dimensionality of Space-Time
                %strong 43
                (1979) 553 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.43.553"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.43.553
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Creutz"}> Michael Creutz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Monte Carlo study of quantized
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                    gauge theory
                %strong 21
                (1980) 2308-2315 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.21.2308"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.21.2308
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://thy.phy.bnl.gov/~creutz/mypubs/pub037.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Creutz"}> Michael Creutz
                ,
                %em Monte Carlo study of renormalization in lattice gauge theory
                Phys.Rev. D
                %strong 23
                (1981) 1815 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.23.1815"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.23.1815
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack" do
                  %a{:href => "http://thy.phy.bnl.gov/~creutz/mypubs/pub045.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Creutz"}> Michael Creutz
                , Laurence Jacobs, Claudio Rebbi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monte Carlo computations in lattice gauge theories
                %strong 95
                4 (1983) 201-282 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-1573(83)90016-9"}> doi:10.1016/0370-1573(83)90016-9
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://thy.phy.bnl.gov/~creutz/mypubs/pub068.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Specifically computation of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap+problem"} mass gap problem
          %ul
            %li#Durr09
              %p S. Durr, Z. Fodor, J. Frison, C. Hoelbling, R. Hoffmann, S.D. Katz, S. Krieg, T. Kurth, L. Lellouch, T. Lippert, K.K. Szabo, G. Vulvert,
              %p
                %em> Ab-initio Determination of Light Hadron Masses
                ,
              %p
                Science 322:1224-1227, 2008 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.3599"}> arXiv:0906.3599
                )
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#FodorHoelbling12"} Fodor-Hoelbling 12, section V of
            %li
              %p
                Sasa Prelovsek:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lattice QCD calculations of hadron spectroscopy
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Particle+Physics"} Encyclopedia of Particle Physics
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.10002"}> arXiv:2505.10002
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion specifically of numerical computation of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/form+factors"} form factors
          %ul
            %li
              B.B. Brandt, S. Capitani, M. Della Morte, D. Djukanovic, J. Gegelia, G. von Hippel, A. Juttner, B. Knippschild, H.B. Meyer, H. Wittig,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Form factors in lattice QCD
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1106.1554"} arXiv:1106.1554
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+networks"} tensor networks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luca+Tagliacozzo"}> Luca Tagliacozzo
                , Alessio Celi, Maciej Lewenstein,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tensor Networks for Lattice Gauge Theories with continuous groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.4811"} arXiv:1405.4811
            %li#BBCCCDFJLMMRRTVV19
              %p
                M.C. Bañuls, R. Blatt, J. Catani, A. Celi, J.I. Cirac, M. Dalmonte, L. Fallani, K. Jansen, M. Lewenstein, S. Montangero, C.A. Muschik, B. Reznik, E. Rico,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luca+Tagliacozzo"} Luca Tagliacozzo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Verstraete"} Frank Verstraete
              %p
                %em Simulating Lattice Gauge Theories within Quantum Technologies
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.00003"}> arXiv:1911.00003
                )
          %p
            On potential implementation of lattice QCD on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computers"} quantum computers
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edison+M.+Murairi"}> Edison M. Murairi
              , Michael J. Cervia, Hersh Kumar, Paulo F. Bedaque, Andrei Alexandru:
              = succeed "," do
                %em How many quantum gates do gauge theories require?
              %strong 106
              (2022) 094504 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.11789"}> arXiv:2208.11789
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.106.094504"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.106.094504
          %h3#renormalization Renormalization
          %p
            A proposal for a rigorous formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            in lattice gauge theory is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadeusz+Balaban"}> Tadeusz Balaban
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Renormalization group approach to lattice gauge field theories: I. Generation of effective actions in a small field approximation and a coupling constant renormalization in four dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007%2FBF01215223"} web
            %li
              %p …
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Dimock"}> Jonathan Dimock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The renormalization group according to Balaban, I. Small fields
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X13300100"} doi:10.1142/S0129055X13300100
            %li
              %p …
          %h3#topological_effects_and_instantons Topological effects and instantons
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            in lattice QCD:
          %ul
            %li#Gruber13
              Florian Gruber,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topology in dynamical Lattice QCD simulations
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://epub.uni-regensburg.de/27631/"} web
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://epub.uni-regensburg.de/27631/1/dissertation.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Jing-Yuan Chen,
                %em Instanton Density Operator in Lattice QCD from Higher Category Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.06673"}> arXiv:2406.06673
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Peng Zhang, Jing-Yuan Chen:
                %em An Explicit Categorical Construction of Instanton Density in Lattice Yang-Mills Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.07195"}> arXiv:2411.07195
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ForSuperYangMills For super Yang-Mills theories
          %p
            Lattice simulation of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactifications"} KK-compactifications
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/10d+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} 10d super Yang-Mills theory
            and numerical test of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
          %h4#general_2 General
          %ul
            %li#Joseph15
              %p
                Anosh Joseph,
                %em Review of Lattice Supersymmetry and Gauge-Gravity Duality
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.01440"}> arXiv:1509.01440
                )
            %li#Hanada16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masanori+Hanada"}> Masanori Hanada
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What lattice theorists can do for superstring/M-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.05421"} arXiv:1604.05421
          %h4#ReferencesBFSS
            Compactification to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 1
          %p
            The
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Veselin G. Filev, Denjoe O’Connor,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The BFSS model on the lattice
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01366"} arXiv:1506.01366
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masanori+Hanada"}> Masanori Hanada
                , Paul Romatschke,
                %em Lattice Simulations of 10d Yang-Mills toroidally compactified to 1d, 2d and 4d
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.06395"}> arXiv:1612.06395
                )
          %p
            Including the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Hrant Gharibyan,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masanori+Hanada"} Masanori Hanada
                %em Toward simulating Superstring/M-theory on a quantum computer
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.06573"}> arXiv:2011.06573
                )
            %li
              %p
                Georg Bergner, Norbert Bodendorfer, Masanori Hanada, Stratos Pateloudis, Enrico Rinaldi, Andreas Schäfer, Pavlos Vranas,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiromasa+Watanabe"} Hiromasa Watanabe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Confinement/deconfinement transition in the D0-brane matrix model – A signature of M-theory?
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.01312"} arXiv:2110.01312
          %h4#ReferencesIKKT
            Compactification to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D= 0
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/IKKT+matrix+model"} IKKT matrix model
            and claims that it predicts spontaneous
